{
  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "All four limbs of POL-NS-01 are made out on this record, so the baseline cancellation fee is chargeable. (a) The trip record carries a driver 'arrived' event at 12:41:50. (b) The 100%-coverage GPS trace places the driver inside the pickup geofence from that same timestamp. (c) He then held position for a continuous in-geofence dwell of 340 seconds, 40 seconds beyond the 300-second minimum for this zone class. (d) The trip was terminated by the driver at 12:47:30 under reason code RIDER_UNREACHABLE, after the dwell had elapsed, with no boarding event recorded.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-TRIP-00204", "EV-GPS-00204", "EV-FARE-00204"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-01"],
      "relies_on": "derived.arrival.longest_qualifying_run.duration_sec",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The arrival geofence test in POL-NS-02 is met on the wider radius this zone class allows: pickup_zone_class is LARGE_VENUE, so the arrival radius is 120 m rather than 50 m, and the driver's own track records a closest approach of 94.94 m to the pin with 35 consecutive qualifying in-radius fixes spanning the dwell.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-00204", "EV-TRIP-00204"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-02"],
      "relies_on": "derived.driver_track.min_distance_m",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "There is no waiting-period shortfall, and therefore no premature cancellation under POL-NS-06: the measured in-geofence dwell is 340 seconds against the LARGE_VENUE minimum of 300 seconds, a surplus of 40 seconds, so the refund route built on a shortfall is not engaged and cannot refund this fee.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-00204", "EV-TRIP-00204"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-06", "POL-NS-01"],
      "relies_on": "derived.arrival.shortfall_sec",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The arrival marker is genuine, so the false-arrival route in POL-NS-05 does not open: at the 12:41:50 arrival timestamp the driver was already inside the arrival radius and not more than 300 m from the pin, and he is stationary at 0.0 km/h throughout the in-geofence dwell, so he was not in motion on an expressway or arterial road when the marker was set.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-00204", "EV-TRIP-00204"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-05"],
      "relies_on": "derived.driver_track.distinct_speeds_kph",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "This is not a wrong-entrance case under POL-NS-03: that clause reaches only a driver stationary outside the POL-NS-02 arrival radius, and the trace places this driver inside the 120 m radius, at a closest approach of 94.94 m, for the whole dwell.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-00204", "EV-TRIP-00204"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-03"],
      "relies_on": "derived.driver_track.min_distance_m",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The POL-NS-07 anti-farming guard does not trip on this driver, so compensation is not withheld on that ground and the case does not escalate under POL-NS-09(d): the guard requires BOTH no_show_terminations_30d of 4 or more AND a rate above 0.08, and the recorded trailing-30-day figure is 3, so the first limb fails.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-DPROF-00204"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-07"],
      "relies_on": "driver_profile.no_show_terminations_30d",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "Where the fee stands, POL-NS-07 fixes the driver's compensation at 80 percent of the SGD 4.00 fee, namely SGD 3.20, with the residual 20 percent retained as platform service fee; that is exactly the figure the payments ledger already computes, and it is the amount the ruling should carry as driver_compensation_sgd.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-FARE-00204"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-07", "POL-GEN-03"],
      "relies_on": "derived.money.driver_compensation",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The fee line is arithmetically sound and carries no integrity defect: fee_schedule.resolution_rule takes the greater of the LARGE_VENUE zone fee (SGD 4.00) and the RYDE_X vehicle-tier fee (SGD 4.00), and fare_breakdown.cancellation_fee records exactly SGD 4.00, so POL-NS-08(d) is not engaged.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-FARE-00204"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-08", "POL-NS-01"],
      "relies_on": "derived.money.fee_charged",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The bundle the driver relies on is clean at weight 1.0 — the trip record, GPS trace, chat log and fare breakdown each carry admissibility status COMPLETE with no issue codes, the trace has zero gaps and 100 percent coverage, and the chat log holds all three messages its own count records — so there is no POL-NS-08(a)-(d) impairment and POL-GEN-02 caps nothing here.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-TRIP-00204", "EV-GPS-00204", "EV-CHAT-00204", "EV-FARE-00204"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-GEN-02", "POL-NS-08"],
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The rider's account of where she stood is internally inconsistent and should be weighed accordingly: her dispute claim says she was standing at the Entrance 1 PHV pickup point the whole time, while the only message she sent identifying her position, at 12:41:05, reads 'entrance 3 phv pickup point', which is also the entrance named in trip_record.pickup.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-CHAT-00204", "EV-TRIP-00204"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-04"],
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    }
  ]
}

{
  "ruling": {
    "ruling": "FULL_REFUND",
    "amount_sgd": 4.0,
    "driver_compensation_sgd": null,
    "referrals": [],
    "confidence": 0.92,
    "explanation": "Rider and driver: the disputed SGD 4.00 cancellation fee cannot stand on this record, and it is refunded in full to the rider.\n\nThe driver's arrival and dwell are not the problem. The trip record shows an 'arrived' event at 12:41:50 (limb (a)), the GPS trace places the driver 94.94 m from the pin — inside the 120 m LARGE_VENUE arrival radius — from that same timestamp (limb (b)), he then held position for a continuous 340-second in-geofence dwell, 40 seconds over the 300-second minimum (limb (c)), and the trip was terminated by the driver at 12:47:30 under RIDER_UNREACHABLE with no boarding event (limb (d)). So POL-NS-01 is made out on its four limbs. But POL-NS-01 charges the fee only where no clause from POL-NS-03 to POL-NS-06 displaces it, and POL-NS-04 does.\n\nPOL-NS-04 is satisfied on all three limbs. (a) The 12:41:05 message, 'hi im at the entrance 3 phv pickup point, which car ah?', both states the rider's own position and entrance and asks for the driver's; the 12:44:40 message, 'boss? i still cannot see u leh', is a statement that she cannot see the vehicle. Both are locating/coordinating messages sent inside the waiting window. (b) The chat log contains no driver message at any point — the middle entry is the platform's own 'Your driver has arrived' system notice, not a reply — and trip_record.in_app_calls is empty, so the driver neither replied within 120 seconds nor made an in-app call before terminating. (c) The rider track's 105 fixes, all qualifying, sit within a maximum of 39.93 m of the pin (mean 21.08 m), well inside the 150 m LARGE_VENUE presence radius, for every fix rather than merely the majority. The clause therefore applies, and its own words fix the result: the rider is exonerated, the cancellation fee is refunded in full, and no driver compensation is payable.\n\nOn the driver's claims: POL-NS-01 is made out but displaced by POL-NS-04, so it does not carry the fee. The SGD 3.20 compensation under POL-NS-07 does not arise, because compensation is payable only where POL-NS-01 stands and no clause from POL-NS-03 to POL-NS-06 displaces it. POL-NS-02 (geofence met), POL-NS-03 (wrong-entrance band not reached — the driver never fell in the 120–400 m band), POL-NS-05 (marker genuine, driver stationary) and POL-NS-06 (no shortfall) are each correctly analysed, and each simply confirms the fee is decided by POL-NS-04 rather than by them. The anti-farming guard under POL-NS-07 does not trip (no_show_terminations_30d is 3, below the 4 required, and 3/142 = 0.021, below 0.08), so no escalation follows from it. The fee line is arithmetically sound — the greater of the SGD 4.00 LARGE_VENUE zone-class fee and the SGD 4.00 RYDE_X tier fee — so POL-NS-08(d) is not engaged. The 'Entrance 1' reference in the rider's filed narrative against 'Entrance 3' in the contemporaneous chat message and trip record is immaterial: limb (c) is a distance test, and the rider's device stayed within 40 m of the pin throughout.\n\nNo POL-NS-09 trigger fires: both counterparty dispute counters are 0, rider no-show disputes in 30 days is 0, the sole-evidence limb is not engaged, and confidence is well above the 0.70 floor. No clause produces a referral, so referrals is empty. The refund moves only the contested cancellation-fee line of SGD 4.00; the SGD 0.50 platform fee is not contested and is not touched. Confidence is capped at 1.0 — the deciding facts rest on the trip record, GPS trace and chat log, each at weight_multiplier 1.0 — and I set it at 0.92."
  },
  "discarded_claims": []
}

{
  "ruling": {
    "ruling": "FULL_REFUND",
    "amount_sgd": 4.0,
    "driver_compensation_sgd": null,
    "referrals": [],
    "confidence": 0.9,
    "explanation": "To the rider: the SGD 4.00 cancellation fee is refunded in full. You were at the pickup point — your device stayed within a 40 m radius of the pin for every one of the 105 qualifying GPS fixes across the window (max 39.93 m, mean 21.08 m, speed 0.0 kph), well inside the 150 m LARGE_VENUE rider-presence radius. You sent two messages: 'hi im at the entrance 3 phv pickup point, which car ah?' at 12:41:05 and 'boss? i still cannot see u leh' at 12:44:40, the second squarely inside the window between the driver's arrival tap (12:41:50) and his cancellation (12:47:30). The driver read both — at 12:41:22 and 12:44:52 — but posted no reply in the chat log and made no in-app call (trip_record.in_app_calls is empty, and there is no driver message anywhere in the log). All three limbs of POL-NS-04 are therefore met: a locating/coordinating message was sent, the driver neither replied within 120 seconds nor called, and your device was inside the presence radius for the whole window. On those limbs the clause itself fixes the outcome — the fee is refunded in full and no driver compensation is payable. The SGD 0.50 platform fee is not part of the contested amount and is not refunded.\n\nTo the driver: your dwell arithmetic is not in issue, and I accept it. The GPS trace puts you inside the 120 m LARGE_VENUE arrival radius, at a closest approach of 94.94 m, holding position for a single continuous in-geofence run of 340 seconds against the 300 second minimum; the 12:41:50 arrival marker was genuine (0.0 km/h, inside the radius), the trip was terminated by you at 12:47:30 under RIDER_UNREACHABLE, and the fare line reconciles (the greater of the SGD 4.00 LARGE_VENUE zone fee and the SGD 4.00 RYDE_X tier fee is SGD 4.00, exactly the amount charged). So the false-arrival route in POL-NS-05, the shortfall route in POL-NS-06, the wrong-entrance route in POL-NS-03 and the fare-integrity check in POL-NS-08(d) all fail to engage, and POL-NS-01's four limbs are made out. But POL-NS-01 charges the fee only 'where all four conditions hold and no clause from POL-NS-03 to POL-NS-06 displaces them', and POL-NS-04 is one of those clauses. Because you made neither a chat reply nor a call while parked inside the radius, POL-NS-04 displaces the charge: the fee is refunded and the SGD 3.20 compensation figure your side points to in the ledger is not paid. No POL-NS-03(ii) pin-ambiguity goodwill arises either, since that clause reaches only a driver stationary outside the arrival radius, and you were inside it.\n\nThe rider's filed narrative says 'Entrance 1' while her 12:41:05 message and trip_record.pickup both say 'Entrance 3'. I note the discrepancy but it does not move the result: POL-NS-04 limb (c) is a distance test measured from the pin, and the rider's device never left a 40 m radius of it.\n\nNo escalation trigger fires. There is no direct contradiction between admissible artifacts on arrival, dwell or rider presence; rider_profile.disputes_with_counterparty_90d and driver_profile.disputes_with_counterparty_90d are both 0; the POL-NS-07 anti-farming count is 3, below the threshold of 4 (and its second limb, a rate above 0.08, is not reached); rider_profile.no_show_disputes_30d is 0; and no deciding artifact is impaired. Every artifact carrying the deciding facts — trip record, GPS trace, chat log and fare breakdown — carries weight_multiplier 1.0 with no issue codes, so the confidence cap is 1.0 and I set confidence at 0.90.",
    "referrals": []
  },
  "discarded_claims": []
}
